# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DiwaliDrops — environment variables
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values for local development,
# OR set these in the Vercel project settings for production.
#
# DO NOT commit real secrets. `.env.local` and `.env` are gitignored.
#
# These credentials come from an Upstash Redis store. You get them either:
#   - automatically, via the Vercel + Upstash Marketplace integration
#     (Vercel injects them into the project for you), or
#   - manually, by copying the REST URL + TOKEN from the Upstash console
#     (https://console.upstash.com).
#
# The app accepts EITHER naming pair below — you only need ONE pair.
# If the Vercel/Upstash integration is used, the KV_* names are injected
# automatically. If you create the store yourself, the UPSTASH_* names are
# the ones shown in the Upstash console.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Option A — Upstash console naming (copy these from console.upstash.com):
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# Option B — Vercel integration naming (auto-injected by the Vercel + Upstash
# Marketplace integration; set manually only if you prefer these names):
# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: If NONE of the variables above are set, the app falls back to an
# in-memory counter. This is fine for local development/preview, but it is
# NOT safe for production: the counter resets whenever the server restarts,
# so the global "never repeat until all 300 are shown" guarantee will break.
# Always configure Upstash Redis before a real event.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
